From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 06n-arch <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:15:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 49/57] panvk: Fold per-copy GS computations into the VS too
 (06n-arch)

UE4's one-pass point light shadows (Deep Rock Galactic under D3D12)
use a GS that, for each of the 6 cube faces, transforms each vertex's
world position by that face's view-projection matrix (from a root CBV)
and emits the triangle to that face's layer if it passes a frustum test.
0029 only folds outputs that are copies of an input or constants, so
every shadow-depth pipeline failed and UE4 bailed out.

Generalize the matcher: each output of vertex j of copy k may be any
computation of in[j], push constants, read-only memory, constants and
ALU ops, as long as it is the same computation for every vertex of the
copy (checked structurally, in[j] standing in for in[0]). The fold
clones copy k's vertex-0 computation into the VS with the VS's own
outputs as its input, and selects between copies on the copy index.
Emits may sit in ifs; the conditions are ignored, since a GS that skips
a copy (UE4's per-face culling) only saves work the rasterizer's
clipping makes up for.
